<title>FINLAND: FINNAIR , BRAATHENS IN STOCKHOLM-OSLO COOP.</title>
<headline>FINNAIR , BRAATHENS IN STOCKHOLM-OSLO COOP.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish national airline Finnair Oy said on Friday it would set six new flights between the Swedish capital Stockholm and Norway's Oslo, expanding its code-sharing cooperation with Norwegian airline Braathens.</p>
<p>&quot;The route will be served with six joint code share return flights a day,&quot; Finnair said in a statement, adding that the flights would begin on August 18.</p>
<p>The schedule will give connections to and from Finnair's domestic routes between Helsinki and Tampere, Vaasa and Turku.</p>
<p>Finnair already has three daily return flights between Helsinki and Oslo, two non-stop and one via Stockholm, it said.</p>
